Chapter: UiFontCceOrder
  cites UI chapter Font
  cites Game chapter Rasterizer
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 CCE orders letters by English frequency (lowercase e t a o i n s h r d l c
 u m w f g y p b v k j x q z at 13-38, uppercase the same at 39-64) and
 `font-glyph` indexes the list by POSITION, so a font whose letters are
 stored alphabetically draws the wrong one for every letter. `font-5x7`
 did, and the browser drew "Hello" as "Hakkd" for a week without anything
 going red: digits, punctuation and spacing were all correct, and capital H
 is 8th in both orderings so it maps to itself.

 This renders through `font-draw-text` and reads the pixels back, so it
 fails on the ordering rather than on anything about a display. Reading the
 art is the point: a wrong permutation still prints a well-formed letter.

Section: Test

  row-text : Framebuf, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  row-text (fb) (y) (x) (x1) =
    if x >= x1 then ""
    else (if fb-get fb x y == 0 then "." else "#") & row-text fb y (x + 1) x1

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let fb = fb-new 24 7 0
    in let drawn = font-draw-text fb font-5x7 "Hea" 0 0 1 0
    in act
      print-line-uni (row-text drawn 0 0 18)
      print-line-uni (row-text drawn 1 0 18)
      print-line-uni (row-text drawn 2 0 18)
      print-line-uni (row-text drawn 3 0 18)
      print-line-uni (row-text drawn 4 0 18)
      print-line-uni (row-text drawn 5 0 18)
      print-line-uni (row-text drawn 6 0 18)
    end
  end
